# name: test_help_messages[bundle.execute]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root bundle execute [OPTIONS] IDENTIFIER [ARGUMENTS]... [global         
   options] [connection options]                                                  
                                                                                  
   Executes a code bundle at the given entrypoint.                                
                                                                                  
   Any additional arguments after the known options will be passed to the code    
   bundle. For example: snow bundle execute my_bundle --entrypoint src/main.py -- 
   --custom-arg value                                                             
                                                                                  
  +- Arguments ------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | *    identifier      TEXT            Identifier of the code bundle; for      |
  |                                      example: MY_CODE_BUNDLE                 |
  |                                      [required]                              |
  |      arguments       [ARGUMENTS]...  Arguments forwarded to the code bundle. |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | *  --entrypoint              TEXT  Entrypoint file path within the code      |
  |                                    bundle.                                   |
  |                                    [required]                                |
  |    --execution-name          TEXT  Name to assign to this code bundle        |
  |                                    execution.                                |
  |    --async                         Run the bundle execution asynchronously   |
  |                                    and return the query ID immediately.      |
  |    --help            -h            Show this message and exit.               |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[bundle.history]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root bundle history [OPTIONS] [global options] [connection options]     
                                                                                  
   Returns the execution history of code bundles.                                 
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --bundle-name                     TEXT     Filter the history to a specific  |
  |                                            code bundle name.                 |
  | --bundle-database                 TEXT     Filter the history to code        |
  |                                            bundles in the given database.    |
  | --bundle-schema                   TEXT     Filter the history to code        |
  |                                            bundles in the given schema.      |
  | --entrypoint                      TEXT     Filter the history to executions  |
  |                                            with the given entrypoint.        |
  | --start-time-range-start          TEXT     Filter the history to executions  |
  |                                            that started at or after this     |
  |                                            timestamp.                        |
  | --start-time-range-end            TEXT     Filter the history to executions  |
  |                                            that started at or before this    |
  |                                            timestamp.                        |
  | --bundle-types                    TEXT     Filter the history to the given   |
  |                                            bundle types. Can be specified    |
  |                                            multiple times.                   |
  | --compute-types                   TEXT     Filter the history to the given   |
  |                                            compute types. Can be specified   |
  |                                            multiple times.                   |
  | --language-types                  TEXT     Filter the history to the given   |
  |                                            language types. Can be specified  |
  |                                            multiple times.                   |
  | --status                          TEXT     Filter the history to executions  |
  |                                            with the given status.            |
  | --execution-name                  TEXT     Filter the history to the         |
  |                                            execution with the given name.    |
  | --result-limit                    INTEGER  Maximum number of history rows to |
  |                                            return.                           |
  |                                            [default: 100]                    |
  | --help                    -h               Show this message and exit.       |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
