# name: test_help_messages[dcm.refresh]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root dcm refresh [OPTIONS] [IDENTIFIER] [global options] [connection    
   options]                                                                       
                                                                                  
   Refreshes dynamic tables defined in DCM project. It applies only to deployed   
   objects.                                                                       
                                                                                  
  +- Arguments ------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |   identifier      [IDENTIFIER]  Identifier of DCM Project. Example:          |
  |                                 MY_DB.MY_SCHEMA.MY_PROJECT. Supports fully   |
  |                                 qualified (recommended) or simple names. If  |
  |                                 unqualified, it defaults to the connection's |
  |                                 database and schema. Optional if --target or |
  |                                 default_target is defined in the manifest.   |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --from                 PATH  Local directory path containing DCM project     |
  |                              files. Omit to use current directory.           |
  | --target               TEXT  Target profile from manifest.yml to use. Uses   |
  |                              default_target if not specified.                |
  | --save-output                Save command response and artifacts to local    |
  |                              'out/' directory.                               |
  | --help         -h            Show this message and exit.                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[dcm.test]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root dcm test [OPTIONS] [IDENTIFIER] [global options] [connection       
   options]                                                                       
                                                                                  
   Tests a DCM project: checks expectations (default/--expectations), runs test   
   scripts in an isolated environment (--script/--all-scripts), or both.          
                                                                                  
  +- Arguments ------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |   identifier      [IDENTIFIER]  Identifier of DCM Project. Example:          |
  |                                 MY_DB.MY_SCHEMA.MY_PROJECT. Supports fully   |
  |                                 qualified (recommended) or simple names. If  |
  |                                 unqualified, it defaults to the connection's |
  |                                 database and schema. Optional if --target or |
  |                                 default_target is defined in the manifest.   |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --from                  PATH  Local directory path containing DCM project    |
  |                               files. Omit to use current directory.          |
  | --variable      -D      TEXT  Variables for the execution context; for       |
  |                               example: -D "<key>=<value>".                   |
  | --expectations                Checks expectations defined in the DCM project |
  |                               against its already-deployed objects. This is  |
  |                               the default when neither --script nor          |
  |                               --all-scripts is given, and may be combined    |
  |                               with either to also run this check.            |
  | --target                TEXT  Target profile from manifest.yml to use. Uses  |
  |                               default_target if not specified.               |
  | --save-output                 Save command response and artifacts to local   |
  |                               'out/' directory.                              |
  | --help          -h            Show this message and exit.                    |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Usage notes ----------------------------------------------------------------+
  | The snow dcm test command runs all expectations (data metric functions)      |
  | defined in your DCM project object. Expectations are data quality rules that |
  | validate conditions on your tables.                                          |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run this command after your tasks and dynamic tables have finished           |
  | processing new data. TEST evaluates the current state of the data in your    |
  | environment, so running it before your pipelines have processed the latest   |
  | transformation logic may produce results that don't reflect your latest      |
  | changes.                                                                     |
  |                                                                              |
  | The command returns:                                                         |
  |                                                                              |
  | • Exit code 0 if all tests pass                                              |
  | • Exit code 1 if any test fails                                              |
  |                                                                              |
  | Use the --save-output option to save the test results to a local             |
  | out/test.json file.                                                          |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Examples -------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | Test all expectations in a DCM project object, where the project name is     |
  | specified in the default_target property in the manifest:                    |
  | snow dcm test                                                                |
  |                                                                              |
  | Test all expectations in a DCM project where the project name is specified   |
  | in the DEV target in the manifest:                                           |
  | snow dcm test --target DEV                                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Test all expectations in a DCM project object with an explicit fully         |
  | qualified name:                                                              |
  | snow dcm test MY_DB.MY_SCHEMA.MY_PROJECT                                     |
  |                                                                              |
  | Test and save the results to the out/ directory:                             |
  | snow dcm test --save-output                                                  |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Related topics -------------------------------------------------------------+
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/index          |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   data-pipelines/dcm-projects                                                |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/dcm-commands/overview                                    |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/dcm-projects/                     |
  |   dcm-projects-overview                                                      |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/dcm-projects/                     |
  |   dcm-projects-pipelines#label-dcm-projects-pipelines-test                   |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[dcm]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root dcm [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...                                    
                                                                                  
   Manages DCM Projects in Snowflake.                                             
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --help  -h        Show this message and exit.                                |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Commands -------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | create             Creates a DCM Project in Snowflake.                       |
  | deploy             Deploys local project changes to Snowflake by creating,   |
  |                    altering, or dropping objects to match your definition    |
  |                    files.                                                    |
  | describe           Provides a description of a DCM Project.                  |
  | drop               Drops a DCM Project. All the objects deployed and managed |
  |                    by this project won't be dropped.                         |
  | drop-deployment    Drops a deployment from the DCM Project.                  |
  | list               Lists all available DCM Projects.                         |
  | list-deployments   Lists deployments of a given DCM Project.                 |
  | plan               Shows what objects would be created, altered, or dropped  |
  |                    by the deploy command, without applying any changes.      |
  | purge              Drops all the objects managed by the DCM Project, but     |
  |                    does not drop the project itself.                         |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[feature.apply]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root feature apply [OPTIONS] [global options] [connection options]      
                                                                                  
   Apply the discovered (or explicit) plan against Snowflake.                     
                                                                                  
   A pure plan-file consumer: auto-discovers the latest unapplied plan under      
   <project_root>/out/plan/ (or consumes --plan <path>). Run snow feature plan    
   first to produce a plan file.                                                  
                                                                                  
   Templating overrides are a plan-time concern only: they are resolved and baked 
   into the plan JSON, so apply does not accept them. Re-run snow feature plan    
   with the new override, then apply.                                             
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --from                 PATH  Local directory containing the feature-store    |
  |                              project (must contain manifest.yml). Omit to    |
  |                              use the current directory.                      |
  | --target               TEXT  Target profile from manifest.yml to use. Uses   |
  |                              default_target when not specified.              |
  | --destructive                Allow operations that drop, recreate, or        |
  |                              overwrite existing objects.                     |
  | --plan                 TEXT  Path to a pre-computed plan JSON file (from     |
  |                              'snow feature plan'). When provided, skips the  |
  |                              auto-discovery of out/plan/.                    |
  | --help         -h            Show this message and exit.                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
