# name: test_help_messages[feature.plan]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root feature plan [OPTIONS] [global options] [connection options]       
                                                                                  
   Show what would change if the project were applied (read-only).                
                                                                                  
   Also writes the plan as JSON under <project_root>/out/plan/ so it can be       
   applied later with snow feature apply.                                         
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --from                       PATH  Local directory containing the            |
  |                                    feature-store project (must contain       |
  |                                    manifest.yml). Omit to use the current    |
  |                                    directory.                                |
  | --target                     TEXT  Target profile from manifest.yml to use.  |
  |                                    Uses default_target when not specified.   |
  | --variable   -D              TEXT  Variables for the project's templating    |
  |                                    context, e.g. -D "<key>=<value>". May be  |
  |                                    repeated.                                 |
  | --out                        TEXT  Path to write the plan JSON file.         |
  |                                    Defaults to                               |
  |                                    <project_root>/out/plan/feature_plan_<ti… |
  | --no-delete      --delete          Deletion detection is OFF by default:     |
  |                                    objects present in the target but absent  |
  |                                    from the manifest are left untouched.     |
  |                                    Pass --delete to enable full-sync         |
  |                                    deletion (emit DROP ops for orphans).     |
  |                                    [default: no-delete]                      |
  | --help       -h                    Show this message and exit.               |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
