  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[feature.sync]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root feature sync [OPTIONS] [global options] [connection options]       
                                                                                  
   Pull deployed feature-store objects into the local sources tree.               
                                                                                  
   Requires an existing manifest.yml and an initialised feature store; unlike     
   init it does not re-bootstrap the runtime. Use --name to sync a single object; 
   --yaml emits YAML instead of .py.                                              
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --from            PATH  Local directory containing the feature-store project |
  |                         (must contain manifest.yml). Omit to use the current |
  |                         directory.                                           |
  | --target          TEXT  Target profile from manifest.yml to use. Uses        |
  |                         default_target when not specified.                   |
  | --name            TEXT  Exact name of a single object to sync                |
  |                         (case-insensitive). Matches across all object kinds  |
  |                         (Entity, BatchSource, StreamingSource,               |
  |                         BatchFeatureView, StreamingFeatureView,              |
  |                         FeatureGroup).  Omit to sync all deployed objects.   |
  | --python                Export deployed objects as .py files (Pydantic       |
  |                         constructors).  This is the default form; pass       |
  |                         --yaml to export YAML instead.                       |
  | --yaml                  Export deployed objects as YAML files instead of the |
  |                         default .py Pydantic constructors.                   |
  | --help    -h            Show this message and exit.                          |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[feature]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root feature [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...                                
                                                                                  
   Manages declarative feature-store objects in Snowflake.                        
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --help  -h        Show this message and exit.                                |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Commands -------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | apply            Apply the discovered (or explicit) plan against Snowflake.  |
  | describe         Describe a single feature-store object.                     |
  | ingest           Ingest records into a streaming feature source via the      |
  |                  Online Service.                                             |
  | init             Bootstrap a feature-store project and pull deployed         |
  |                  artifacts.                                                  |
  | list             List deployed feature-store objects from Snowflake.         |
  | online-service   Manages the feature store online service.                   |
  | plan             Show what would change if the project were applied          |
  |                  (read-only).                                                |
  | query            Query online features for a feature view via the Online     |
  |                  Service.                                                    |
  | sync             Pull deployed feature-store objects into the local sources  |
  |                  tree.                                                       |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[git.copy]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root git copy [OPTIONS] REPOSITORY_PATH DESTINATION_PATH [global        
   options] [connection options]                                                  
                                                                                  
   Copies all files from given state of repository to local directory or stage.   
                                                                                  
   If the source path ends with '/', the command copies contents of specified     
   directory. Otherwise, it creates a new directory or file in the destination    
   directory.                                                                     
                                                                                  
  +- Arguments ------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | *    repository_path       TEXT  Path to git repository stage with scope     |
  |                                  provided. Path to the repository root must  |
  |                                  end with '/'. For example:                  |
  |                                  @my_repo/branches/main/                     |
  |                                  [required]                                  |
  | *    destination_path      TEXT  Target path for copy operation. Should be a |
  |                                  path to a directory on remote stage or      |
  |                                  local file system.                          |
  |                                  [required]                                  |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --parallel          INTEGER  Number of parallel threads to use when          |
  |                              downloading files.                              |
  |                              [default: 4]                                    |
  | --help      -h               Show this message and exit.                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Usage notes ----------------------------------------------------------------+
  | None.                                                                        |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Examples -------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | This example creates a snowcli2.0/ directory on stage @public and copies all |
  | files from the commit marked with tag v2.0.0 into that directory:            |
  | snow git copy @my_snow_git/tags/v2.0.0/ @public/snowcli2.0/                  |
  |                                                                              |
  | The following example creates a plugin_tests directory in the local file     |
  | system and downloads the contents of the tests/plugin directory into it.     |
  | snow git copy @snowcli_git/branches/main/tests/plugin plugin_tests/          |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Related topics -------------------------------------------------------------+
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/index          |
  | • Snowflake CLI command reference                                            |
  |   https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/overview                                                 |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/git-commands/overview                                    |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/git/copy-files |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
