# name: test_help_messages[spcs.compute-pool.set]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root spcs compute-pool set [OPTIONS] NAME [global options] [connection  
   options]                                                                       
                                                                                  
   Sets one or more properties for the compute pool.                              
                                                                                  
  +- Arguments ------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | *    name      TEXT  Identifier of the compute pool; for example:            |
  |                      my_compute_pool                                         |
  |                      [required]                                              |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --min-nodes                  INTEGER RANGE [x>=1]  Minimum number of nodes   |
  |                                                    for the compute pool.     |
  | --max-nodes                  INTEGER RANGE [x>=1]  Maximum number of nodes   |
  |                                                    for the compute pool.     |
  | --auto-resume                                      The compute pool will     |
  |                                                    automatically resume when |
  |                                                    a service or job is       |
  |                                                    submitted to it.          |
  | --no-auto-resume                                   The compute pool will     |
  |                                                    automatically resume when |
  |                                                    a service or job is       |
  |                                                    submitted to it.          |
  | --auto-suspend-secs          INTEGER RANGE [x>=1]  Number of seconds of      |
  |                                                    inactivity after which    |
  |                                                    you want Snowflake to     |
  |                                                    automatically suspend the |
  |                                                    compute pool.             |
  | --comment                    TEXT                  Comment for the compute   |
  |                                                    pool.                     |
  | --help               -h                            Show this message and     |
  |                                                    exit.                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Usage notes ----------------------------------------------------------------+
  | The current role must have MODIFY privilege on the compute pool to set       |
  | properties.                                                                  |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Examples -------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | snow spcs compute-pool set tutorial_compute_pool --min-nodes 2 --max-nodes 4 |
  | Output:                                                                      |
  | +-------------------------------------------+                                |
  | | key    | value                            |                                |
  | |--------+----------------------------------|                                |
