  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/spcs-commands/compute-pool-commands/set                  |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[spcs.compute-pool]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root spcs compute-pool [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...                      
                                                                                  
   Manages Snowpark Container Services compute pools.                             
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --help  -h        Show this message and exit.                                |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Commands -------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | create     Creates a new compute pool.                                       |
  | deploy     Deploys a compute pool from the project definition file.          |
  | describe   Provides description of compute pool.                             |
  | drop       Drops compute pool with given name.                               |
  | list       Lists all available compute pools.                                |
  | resume     Resumes the compute pool from a SUSPENDED state.                  |
  | set        Sets one or more properties for the compute pool.                 |
  | status     Retrieves the status of a compute pool along with a relevant      |
  |            message, if one exists.                                           |
  | stop-all   Deletes all services running on the compute pool.                 |
  | suspend    Suspends the compute pool by suspending all currently running     |
  |            services and then releasing compute pool nodes.                   |
  | unset      Resets one or more properties for the compute pool to their       |
  |            default value(s).                                                 |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[spcs.image-registry.login]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root spcs image-registry login [OPTIONS] [global options] [connection   
   options]                                                                       
                                                                                  
   Logs in to the account image registry with the current user's credentials      
   through Docker.                                                                
                                                                                  
   Must be called from a role that can view at least one image repository in the  
   image registry.                                                                
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --private-link            Get the private link URL instead of the public     |
  |                           URL.                                               |
  | --help          -h        Show this message and exit.                        |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Usage notes ----------------------------------------------------------------+
  | • Docker Desktop must be installed because the command uses docker to log in |
  |   to Snowflake.                                                              |
  | • The current role must have READ privileges for the image repository in the |
  |   account to get the registry URL.                                           |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Examples -------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | snow spcs image-registry login                                               |
  | Output: Login Succeeded                                                      |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Related topics -------------------------------------------------------------+
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/index          |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/overview                                                 |
  | • spcs command reference                                                     |
  |   https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/spcs-commands/overview                                   |
  | • image-repository command reference                                         |
  |   https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/spcs-commands/image-registry-commands/overview           |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/services/      |
  |   manage-images                                                              |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[spcs.image-registry.token]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root spcs image-registry token [OPTIONS] [global options] [connection   
   options]                                                                       
                                                                                  
   Retrieves a registry authentication token based on your current connection.    
                                                                                  
   Note that this token is specific to your current user and will not grant       
   access to any repositories that your current user cannot access.               
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --help  -h        Show this message and exit.                                |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                                                                  
   Usage Example: snow spcs image-registry token --format JSON | docker login     
   $(snow spcs image-registry url) -u 0sessiontoken --password-stdin See the      
   following for how to use this command to authenticate with SSO:                
   https://community.snowflake.com/s/article/Authenticating-with-Snowpark-Contain 
   er-Services-Image-Repository-via-SSO-and-Token-with-Snow-CLI                   
                                                                                  
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Usage notes ----------------------------------------------------------------+
  | None.                                                                        |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Examples -------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | The following example shows how to return the token associated with the      |
  | specified connection that you can use to authenticate with the registry.     |
  | snow spcs image-registry token --connection mytest                           |
  | Output:                                                                      |
  | +--------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
  | | key        | value                                                         |
  | |------------+-------------------------------------------------------------- |
  | | token      | ************************************************************* |
  | |            | ************************************************************* |
  | | expires_in | 3600                                                          |
  | +--------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
  |                                                                              |
  | Example usage with docker:                                                   |
  | snow spcs image-registry token --format=JSON | docker login YOUR_HOST -u     |
  | 0sessiontoken --password-stdin                                               |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Related topics -------------------------------------------------------------+
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/index          |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/overview                                                 |
  | • spcs command reference                                                     |
  |   https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/spcs-commands/overview                                   |
  | • image-repository command reference                                         |
  |   https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/spcs-commands/image-registry-commands/overview           |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/services/      |
  |   manage-images                                                              |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_messages[spcs.image-registry.url]
  '''
                                                                                  
   Usage: root spcs image-registry url [OPTIONS] [global options] [connection     
   options]                                                                       
                                                                                  
   Gets the image registry URL for the current account.                           
                                                                                  
   Must be called from a role that can view at least one image repository in the  
   image registry.                                                                
                                                                                  
  +- Options --------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | --private-link            Get the private link URL instead of the public     |
  |                           URL.                                               |
  | --help          -h        Show this message and exit.                        |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Global and connection options ----------------------------------------------+
  | Connection options: --connection, --host, --port, --protocol, --account,     |
  | --user, --password, --authenticator, --workload-identity-provider,           |
  | --private-key-file, --token, --token-file-path, --database, --schema,        |
  | --role, --warehouse, --temporary-connection, --mfa-passcode, --enable-diag,  |
  | --diag-log-path, --diag-allowlist-path, --oauth-client-id,                   |
  | --oauth-client-secret, --oauth-authorization-url, --oauth-token-request-url, |
  | --oauth-redirect-uri, --oauth-scope, --oauth-disable-pkce,                   |
  | --oauth-enable-refresh-tokens, --oauth-enable-single-use-refresh-tokens,     |
  | --client-store-temporary-credential, --secondary-roles,                      |
  | --server-session-keep-alive                                                  |
  | Global options: --format, --verbose, --debug, --silent,                      |
  | --enhanced-exit-codes, --decimal-precision                                   |
  |                                                                              |
  | Run `snow --help` for full descriptions, or use `--help-all` on this         |
  | command.                                                                     |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Usage notes ----------------------------------------------------------------+
  | The current role must have READ privileges for the image repository in the   |
  | account to get the registry URL.                                             |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Examples -------------------------------------------------------------------+
  | snow spcs image-registry url                                                 |
  | Output: <orgname-acctname>.registry.snowflakecomputing.com                   |
  +------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  +- Related topics -------------------------------------------------------------+
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/index          |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/overview                                                 |
  | • spcs command reference                                                     |
  |   https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/spcs-commands/overview                                   |
  | • image-repository command reference                                         |
  |   https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/               |
  |   command-reference/spcs-commands/image-registry-commands/overview           |
  | • https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/snowflake-cli/services/      |
  |   manage-images                                                              |
